.. par:parameter:: Monitor:level

   :Summary: :s:`Level of information written to stdout`
   :Type:    :par:typefmt:`string`
   :Default: :d:`"medium"`
   :Scope:     :c:`Cello`

   :e:`This parameter controls the verbosity of output during a running simulation. Possible values are "high", "medium", "low", and "none".`

----

.. par:parameter:: Monitor:mute_list

   :Summary: :s:`Which monitor output components to mute`
   :Type:    :par:typefmt:`list ( string )`
   :Default: :d:`[]`
   :Scope:     :c:`Cello`

   :e:`List of monitor output components, such as "Performance", "Solver", "Simulation", to mute. Default is the empty list.`

----

.. par:parameter:: Monitor:only_list

   :Summary: :s:`Which monitor output components to write`
   :Type:    :par:typefmt:`list ( string )`
   :Default: :d:`[]`
   :Scope:     :c:`Cello`

   :e:`List of monitor output components, such as "Performance", "Solver", "Simulation", to include in monitoring output. Analogous to "solo" in audio mixing, if non-empty all components not listed are muted. Default is the empty list: all components are active unless muted.`

----

.. par:parameter:: Monitor:schedule

   :Summary: :s:`Schedule for when to write monitor output`
   :Type:    :par:typefmt:`subgroup`
   :Default: :d:`none`
   :Scope:     :c:`Cello`

   :e:`See the` `schedule`_ :e:`subgroup for parameters to define when to write monitoring output to stdout.` 

